    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Maths feels like a bridge between abstract ideas and real-world logic—something I enjoy solving puzzles for, even if it’s not always intuitive. My parents’ academic backgrounds (one with a PhD) made me curious about patterns, but my part-time job in Naples keeps me grounded in practical applications. It’s both challenging and rewarding, like baking where precision matters but creativity isn’t forbidden.",
